Use a private work folder per process. Upstream puts its temporary files in
/tmp/epsonWork, created 0755 by whoever scans first, so every other user
crashed with SIGSEGV when saving the image: the failure went unnoticed
(mkstemp() checked with !fd) and Saving dereferenced the NULL CESFile.
Create the folder with mkdtemp() under $TMPDIR (or /tmp) instead, fix the
mkstemp() check, a descriptor leak and a buffer one byte too short, and
throw a write error from Saving. /tmp/epsonWork/interrupt.dat is kept: the
prebuilt es2netif uses it for IPC.

